Subject: [PATCH 2/2] audio/avrcp: Don't ask a filesystem folder's item count again

SetBrowsedPlayer and ChangePath responses already carry the number of
items in the folder they lead to, so GetTotalNumberOfItems after them
only delays the next browsing command by a round trip, or by the whole
browsing timeout when the target doesn't answer it. Keep it for the
Now Playing list and search results, which nothing else counts.
---
--- a/profiles/audio/avrcp.c
+++ b/profiles/audio/avrcp.c
@@ -3545,6 +3545,15 @@
 	else
 		player->scope = 0x01;
 
+	/*
+	 * SetBrowsedPlayer and ChangePath responses already carry the number
+	 * of items in a filesystem folder: asking again costs a round trip
+	 * before the next browsing command, and the whole browsing timeout
+	 * when the target doesn't answer.
+	 */
+	if (player->scope == 0x01)
+		return 0;
+
 	avrcp_get_total_numberofitems(session);
 
 	return 0;
